        "submission": "snapshot_suffix_store_independence_knowledge.json",
        "summary": "No further work; the run's investigation is complete with no necessary gaps and no open judgments. Conclusion (sourced and executed): a follower that installs a snapshot at index S while its persisted log still ends above S never accepts the leader's PrevLogEntry=S check and never converges — installSnapshot (raft.go:1814-1953) never truncates above req.LastLogIndex and never calls setLastLog, so getLastEntry (state.go:167-174) keeps returning the stale cached index/term, appendEntries (raft.go:1475-1502) rejects, and replicateTo/sendLatestSnapshot (replication.go:222-260, 299-383) re-send the same snapshot. Evidence: CheckRun 2322bd7884b749f89c3101f04bc82e78 (control holds; case violated, witness 3) and CheckRun ed8023e758ae49bc93676179f4ae489c (monotonic store also violated, witness 5). Limits recorded: single-process in-memory transport/stores, progress only, no safety or restart/recovery claim. This is an unchanged status confirmation, not a stop declaration."
